this combination. Portions whose design derives from the GPL-3.0 work
above remain available under GPL-3.0 at their original source.

No source file from either upstream project is copied into this
repository. The tracking pipeline here is written against the public
`ultralytics` Python API.


Not included from upstream, on purpose
--------------------------------------

- The vendored `ultralytics` 8.0.3 source tree (13,369 lines). This
  project installs `ultralytics` from PyPI instead.
- `deep_sort_pytorch` and its ReID checkpoint, which upstream asked
  users to download from a third-party Google Drive folder. The
  trackers used here (BoT-SORT, ByteTrack) ship with `ultralytics`.
- The two Colab notebooks (10 MB and 16 MB, embedded outputs). One of
  them contained a hard-coded Roboflow API key in plain text. No
  credential from upstream is reproduced here.
